drm/sun4i: add D1/T113 HDMI PHY support

Mainline has the D1/T113 display engine, mixers and TCONs, and the CCU
driver already provides CLK_BUS_HDMI, CLK_HDMI_24M, CLK_HDMI_CEC and the
RST_BUS_HDMI_{MAIN,SUB} resets.  What is missing is the HDMI PHY: the
D1/T113 does not use the Synopsys PHY handled by the A83T and H6 paths,
but a custom Allwinner one with no published documentation.

This is a forward-port of Samuel Holland's out-of-tree work
(github.com/smaeul/linux, branch d1/hdmi-support, commits
"drm/sun4i: sun8i-hdmi-phy: Add support for D1 PHY" and
"[HACK] drm/sun4i: Copy in BSP code for D1 HDMI PHY") from a 6.2-era
tree onto 6.18.  The dw_hdmi_phy_ops interface and phy_force_vendor are
unchanged between those versions, so the port is mechanical; the API
drift in the original commits (of_device.h, drm_crtc_helper.h, the
remove() return type, the sun4i_dotclock rename) is not carried over.

The register layout in aw_phy.h is BSP-derived, which is why this has
never been upstreamable in this form.

Not-Signed-off-by: nobody, this is a downstream hack
